{
  "name": "B · User-loan matching",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "0b0b0b0b-0000-4000-8000-000000000101",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -32,
        -448
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1408,
        "height": 288,
        "content": "## B · User-loan matching (S2 hard filter · S3 cohorts · S4 cache · S5 batched LLM + rule veto)\nTriggered by the signed webhook after ingestion (JWT, 202 at once), by the sweeper for batches that stalled, or by **Run manually** for every batch waiting. One batch at a time, in **two database round trips** when everything is cached:\n1. **Claim batch** (one statement): claim it, so a replay or the sweeper can't match it twice; read `app_config`; find the uncached cohorts. Every pending (pair, fuzzy criterion) collapses to (criterion, banded facts), and cached verdicts are reused. Criteria without a compiled rule are listed too. n8n only ever holds cohorts and criteria, never users × products.\n2. Only if something is uncached: **K cohorts per request** plus one **compile** request through the LLM gateway in one call (it sends them `llm_concurrency` at a time), then **cache** the verdicts and rules.\n3. **Write matches** (one statement): one set-based INSERT of the hard filter joined with the cohort verdicts, then mark the batch matched. A compiled rule can veto an uncertain verdict, never vouch for one. Metrics per stage go to `pipeline_metrics` in the same statements.\n4. Call **Workflow C**.\n\n**To run it from this canvas:** open the chevron on **Execute workflow**, pick **Run manually**, and click. It matches every batch waiting in `ingested`; with none waiting it ends at **Nothing waiting**. `make demo-reset ARGS=\"--cold-batch 1000\"` loads a waiting batch whose cohorts aren't cached, so the run takes every branch, LLM included. Webhook runs from the upload page are under **Executions**."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0b0b0b0b-0000-4000-8000-000000000102",
      "name": "LLM only for what's left",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1568,
        -592
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 960,
        "height": 176,
        "color": 4,
        "content": "### Match-time LLM calls = ⌈uncached cohorts ÷ K⌉ + ⌈uncompiled criteria ÷ 25⌉\nNormally **0**: Workflow A's warm step judges every cohort the products can produce right after each crawl, so batches find them cached. Otherwise flat in the number of users: 10k or 100k users give the same cohorts. 0 on a rerun (everything is cached). Skipped entirely when no product has a fuzzy criterion, or when `match_llm_enabled` is false."
      }
    },
